  "bug": {
    "bug_id": "Math-8",
    "project": "Math",
    "summary": "DiscreteDistribution.sample(int) may throw an exception if first element of singletons of sub-class type",
    "description": "Creating an array with \nArray.newInstance(singletons.get(0).getClass(), sampleSize)\nin DiscreteDistribution.sample(int) is risky. An exception will be thrown if:\n\nsingleons.get(0)\nis of type T1, an sub-class of T, and\n\nDiscreteDistribution.sample()\nreturns an object which is of type T, but not of type T1.\n\nTo reproduce:\n\nList<Pair<\nObject\n,\nDouble\n>> list = \nnew\nArrayList<Pair<\nObject\n, \nDouble\n>>();\nlist.add(\nnew\nPair<\nObject\n, \nDouble\n>(\nnew\n\nObject\n() {}, \nnew\n\nDouble\n(0)));\nlist.add(\nnew\nPair<\nObject\n, \nDouble\n>(\nnew\n\nObject\n() {}, \nnew\n\nDouble\n(1)));\n\nnew\nDiscreteDistribution<\nObject\n>(list).sample(1);\n\nAttaching a patch."
  },
